cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use steph-speak-train, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "steph-speak-train: fine-tuning data for spoken summaries of terminal output"
abstract: >-
  Fine-tuning corpus (SFT and DPO configurations) for steph-speak, a small language model
  that turns a terminal command's output into a short spoken summary for a blind or
  visually impaired person. Real, anonymized command captures in French and English,
  labeled by Qwen3.5-9B and filtered by a two-pass judge of the same model. Companion
  dataset to the Steph Speak Bench evaluation benchmark.
authors:
  - family-names: Parra
    given-names: Luis
version: 0.0.0-draft
date-released: 2026-09-27
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/tutozz/steph"
url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/lsmdx/steph-speak-train"
keywords:
  - dataset
  - accessibility
  - screen reader
  - terminal
  - fine-tuning
  - small language models
  - steph
